---
title: Revision Lifecycle
description: Authorizes immutable-head targeted feedback and child revision lifecycle; Task graph continues to own worker execution.
---
flowchart LR
%% relay: initial none
none["state: NONE"]
requested["state: REQUESTED"]
queued["state: QUEUED"]
running["state: RUNNING"]
verified["state: VERIFIED"]
failed["state: FAILED"]
stale["state: STALE"]
reviewerAuthorized["guard: reviewerAuthorized"]
sameHead["guard: reviewHeadCurrent"]
ownerEligible["guard: originalTaskSucceeded"]
recordRequest["action: revision.recordRequest"]
recordQueue["action: revision.queueTask"]
recordVerified["action: revision.recordVerified"]
recordFailed["action: revision.recordFailed"]
markStaleRequested["action: revision.markStale"]
markStaleQueued["action: revision.markStale"]
markStaleRunning["action: revision.markStale"]
verdictReady["guard: changesRequiredRecorded"]
none -->|on: revision.submit| reviewerAuthorized
reviewerAuthorized -->|true| sameHead
reviewerAuthorized -->|false| none
sameHead -->|true| ownerEligible
sameHead -->|false| none
ownerEligible -->|true| recordRequest
ownerEligible -->|false| none
recordRequest --> requested
%% Duplicate submissions are idempotent only when the durable request payload
%% matches. The reducer rejects a conflicting payload for the same request ID.
requested -->|on: revision.submit| requested
requested -->|on: revision.queue| verdictReady
verdictReady -->|true| recordQueue
verdictReady -->|false| requested
recordQueue --> queued
queued -->|on: revision.started| running
running -->|on: revision.verified| recordVerified
recordVerified --> verified
running -->|on: revision.failed| recordFailed
recordFailed --> failed
requested -->|on: review.head_changed| markStaleRequested
markStaleRequested --> stale
queued -->|on: review.head_changed| markStaleQueued
markStaleQueued --> stale
running -->|on: review.head_changed| markStaleRunning
markStaleRunning --> stale
